#: includes/admin/views/help.php:34
msgid "How Cookie Consent works"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:35
msgid "Close help"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:40
msgid "A visitor arrives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:41
msgid "They see your banner. Until they choose, every non-essential script, video, map and font on the page stays switched off. Only the Necessary ones run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:44
msgid "They make a choice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:45
msgid "Allow all, Deny, or switch on the categories they want and click Allow selection. The things they allowed switch on immediately, without reloading the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:48
msgid "The choice is remembered"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:49
msgid "It is stored in a small cookie called sccm_consent together with a unique consent ID, and saved in your Consent Records as proof. The visitor can see their consent ID and change their choice at any time with the cookie settings button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:52
msgid "Your cookie list keeps itself current"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:53
msgid "A scan looks at your pages. Well-known cookies (Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, YouTube and more) are put in the right category automatically. Anything it does not recognise waits in the Cookies tab for you to approve. Visitors see the list in the Details tab of the banner and on your Cookie Policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:56
msgid "It works with page caching"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:57
msgid "Every visitor gets the same page. The banner and the visitor's choice are handled in their browser, so caching plugins and CDNs keep working. When you save settings or the cookie list changes, the plugin clears the page cache of common caching plugins and hosts (WP Engine, NitroPack, WP Rocket, LiteSpeed, W3 Total Cache, WP Super Cache, WP Fastest Cache, SiteGround, Breeze, Hummingbird). With any other cache or a CDN, clear it once after changing settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:61
msgid "Every tab, button and option explained"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:69
#: includes/admin/views/tab-dashboard.php:102
msgid "Preview banner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:69
msgid "Opens your website with the banner showing, even if you already made a choice yourself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:70
msgid "Switch off / Switch on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:70
msgid "Turns the whole system off or on. When off, visitors see no banner and nothing is blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:71
#: includes/admin/views/tab-dashboard.php:111
msgid "Needs your attention"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:71
msgid "A short to-do list. Each line says what is missing and has one button to fix it. \"Everything looks good\" means there is nothing to do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:72
#: includes/admin/views/tab-dashboard.php:136
msgid "Cookies on your site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:72
msgid "How many cookies are in your list, split by category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:73
msgid "Visitor choices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:73
msgid "How many visitors accepted, rejected or chose custom settings in the last 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:74
msgid "Last scan / Scan now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:74
msgid "When your website was last checked for cookies, and a button to check it again now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:82
msgid "Needs your review"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:82
msgid "Cookies the scan found but could not recognise. Nothing is shown to visitors until you decide. It only appears when something is waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:83
#: includes/admin/views/tab-cookies.php:136
msgid "Approve"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:83
msgid "Choose a category, then click Approve. The cookie joins the list visitors see. (If \"Ask again when the cookie list changes\" is on, visitors are asked again.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:84
msgid "Ignore / Ignore all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:84
msgid "Hides a cookie that is not part of your website, for example one from a browser extension. It is not reported again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:85
#: includes/admin/views/tab-cookies.php:190
#: includes/admin/views/tab-dashboard.php:56
#: includes/admin/views/tab-dashboard.php:184
msgid "Scan now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:85
msgid "Two steps. First the server reads your pages. Small websites (up to 40 pages) are scanned completely; bigger ones get more pages the bigger they are (100 pages → 55, 300 → 72, at most 80): every main page first, one item of each content type, then sub pages and sub-sub pages from every section in turn. Then the same pages open in hidden frames in your own browser (three at a time) with everything allowed, so cookies set by scripts (Google Analytics, HubSpot, chat widgets…) and by embedded services (YouTube, Calendly…) are found too. Nothing is stored for visitors. Known cookies are added automatically. It takes one to two minutes for a big website. You can switch to another browser tab meanwhile; if you leave the page, the server part finishes in the background and the browser part continues the next time you open a Cookie Consent screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:86
msgid "Your cookie list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:86
msgid "Everything visitors see, grouped by category. \"Automatic\" means we added it, \"Added by you\" means you did."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:87
msgid "Edit / Delete"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:87
msgid "Change a cookie's category, provider, purpose or duration, or remove it from the list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:88
#: includes/admin/views/tab-cookies.php:50
#: includes/admin/views/tab-cookies.php:249
msgid "Add a cookie by hand"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:88
msgid "For cookies a scan cannot see. A * in the name matches anything, so _ga_* covers _ga_ABC123."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:89
msgid "Add all cookies of a known service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:89
msgid "Adds the usual cookies of a service such as Google Analytics in one click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:90
msgid "Scan report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:90
msgid "Technical details of the last scan: services found, other third-party files, and pages checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:98
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:70
msgid "Where should the banner appear?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:98
msgid "A bar at the bottom or top, a box in a corner, or a window in the centre of the page. Click the picture that looks right."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:99
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:89
msgid "Banner style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:99
msgid "Compact (default): your text and three buttons, Allow all, Deny and Customize. Customize opens the detailed window. Detailed: the window with tabs opens straight away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:100
msgid "What visitors see"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:100
msgid "The detailed window has three tabs. Consent: your text and a switch per category. Details: every category opens to show the providers and each cookie (what it does, how long it lasts, its type). About: what cookies are, and the visitor's own choice, date and consent ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:101
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:99
msgid "Button order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:101
msgid "Four orders: Allow all · Deny · Allow selection (default), Deny · Allow all · Allow selection, or with \"Allow selection\" in the middle. In the compact style \"Customize\" takes the place of \"Allow selection\". Allow all, Deny and Allow selection always look exactly the same, which is what makes any order fair."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:102
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:110
msgid "Cookie settings button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:102
msgid "A small button visible after the choice, so visitors can change their mind. In a corner it is a round icon. At the bottom centre or on the left or right edge it is a slim tab with the word \"Cookies\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:103
msgid "Colours and rounded corners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:103
msgid "Match the banner to your brand. Accept and Reject always share one style, because valid consent needs both choices to be equally easy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:104
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:148
msgid "Links in the banner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:104
msgid "The Cookie Policy page and your Privacy Policy page, linked in the banner."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:105
#: includes/admin/views/tab-banner.php:168
msgid "Category names and descriptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:105
msgid "Rename a category, rewrite its description, or hide one your website does not need."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:106
msgid "Words in the banner, the cookie details and the consent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:106
msgid "Every sentence and button label visitors see. Leave a field empty to keep the default, which is translated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:107
msgid "Custom CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:107
msgid "For developers: extra styles for the banner. Classes start with sccm-."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:115
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:40
msgid "Remember the choice for"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:115
msgid "How long a visitor is left alone before the banner shows again. Pick a preset or type your own number of days. The longest possible is 395 days, because browsers do not keep a cookie longer. 0 forgets the choice when the browser closes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:116
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:55
msgid "Ask again when the cookie list changes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:116
msgid "If you add a new cookie, visitors agreed to an older list, so they are asked again. A scan that finds nothing new never asks again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:117
msgid "Do not ask again after a Reject"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:117
msgid "A waiting period (in days) after a visitor refuses, so you do not nag them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:118
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:57
msgid "Reload the page when consent is withdrawn"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:118
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:57
msgid "A script that already ran cannot be stopped, so the page reloads to stop it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:119
msgid "Browser privacy signal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:119
msgid "Some browsers send \"do not track me\" (Global Privacy Control). We honour it: the chosen categories stay off, no banner is shown, and the choice is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:120
msgid "Google Consent Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:120
msgid "Tells Google Analytics and Google Ads what the visitor allowed. Strict blocks Google tags until consent. Advanced lets them load without cookies. Leave on Strict unless your marketing team asks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:121
msgid "Google Tag Manager / Analytics ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:121
msgid "Optional. Enter an ID and the plugin loads the tag for you with correct consent handling. Leave empty if your theme or another plugin already adds it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:122
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:104
msgid "Automatic blocking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:122
msgid "Switches off scripts, videos, maps and fonts of known services until the visitor allows their category. \"Known services\" lists what is recognised, and \"Your own blocking rules\" adds more."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:123
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:168
msgid "Scan my website"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:123
msgid "How often your website is checked automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:124
#: includes/admin/views/tab-settings.php:177
msgid "Also learn from visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:124
msgid "Visitors' browsers can report cookies that only JavaScript sets. Only names are sent, never values, never from logged-in users, and only after several visitors report the same cookie."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:125
msgid "Email about cookie changes / Daily check at / Send the email to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:125
msgid "Once a day, at the time you choose, the plugin checks whether anything changed in the last 24 hours: cookies added to the banner, cookies waiting for review, new third-party services. Only then it sends one email; no changes, no email. Scheduled scans run one hour before, so their findings are included. The email goes to the site admin (unless switched off) and up to 10 addresses, one per line. It contains no links into WordPress, because some recipients may not have an account. \"Send me a sample email\" checks delivery; the result of the last email is shown under it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:126
msgid "Consent records"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:126
msgid "Whether to keep a record of every choice, how the visitor's IP address is stored (shortened, as a one-way code, or not at all), and how many months to keep records."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:134
msgid "The table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:134
msgid "One line per choice: when, the consent ID, what they chose, which categories they allowed, whether a privacy signal was used, which cookie-list version they agreed to, and on which page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:135
msgid "Search and filters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:135
msgid "Paste a visitor's consent ID to find their record, or filter by choice or date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:136
msgid "Export CSV"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:136
msgid "Downloads the records (with your current filters) as a spreadsheet file, for audits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:137
msgid "Delete old / Delete all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:137
msgid "Removes records older than your retention period, or every record. Deleting all cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:145
#: includes/admin/views/tab-tools.php:21
msgid "Ask all visitors again"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:145
msgid "Shows the banner to everyone again, for example after you change how you use cookies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:146
msgid "Export / Import settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:146
msgid "Copies all settings and your cookie list to a file, so you can use the same setup on another website."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:147
#: includes/admin/views/tab-tools.php:45
msgid "Delete all data when the plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:147
msgid "Off by default, so your consent records survive. Turn it on only if you want a clean removal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:148
#: includes/admin/views/tab-tools.php:50
msgid "Reset settings to defaults"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:148
msgid "Puts every setting back to how it was at the start. Your cookie list and records are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:149
#: includes/admin/views/tab-tools.php:55
msgid "Developer reference"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:149
msgid "Shortcodes, links and JavaScript you can use in your theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:154
msgid "Words you may meet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:156
#: includes/admin/views/tab-records.php:83
#: includes/admin/views/tab-records.php:84
#: includes/admin/views/tab-records.php:112
msgid "Consent ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/help.php:157
msgid "A random code given to a visitor when they first choose. It identifies their choice, not them: it contains no name or email. They can see it in the About tab of the cookie banner."
